' UVK's DATA lines (data section $30a4c-$49ea9, taken from the program item by item, in its order).
' Patterns for handlers on $42a resvector whose any other first word, and handlers outside $1001-$DFFFFF (in ROM or in
' low memory), where only the address can be tested.
' Read by identify_vector_handler.
' Record format (every item a zero-terminated DATA string):
' count     "" = 3 tests follow, a digit n = n tests follow, "*" = end of the table (nothing found).
' n tests   each one either
' offset, pattern  when offset is 0-2 characters:
' offset "" = the next long of the handler (0, 4, 8 ... counted per record; only "" advances it),
' offset of 1-2 characters = a hex byte offset from the handler start ("8", "c", "10", "3b").
' The long there is turned into 8 upper-case hex digits and compared with the pattern:
' pattern of 1 character = a preset long, by VAL: 0 ????????, 1 08170005, 2 302F0004, 3 41EF0006,
' 4 4E680817, 5 4E560000, 6 3F2E0008, 7 302F000E, 8 4A78059E, 9 42B805A0;
' 3-7 characters without * at either end = hex left-padded with 0 to 8 digits ("4c6d3fc" = 04C6D3FC);
' * first = the digits are the low end, the rest wild ("*43fa" = ????43FA);
' * last = the digits are the high end, the rest wild ("2079*" = 2079????, "223aff*" = 223AFF??);
' 2 or 8 characters = used as they are.
' ? stands for any one hex digit wherever it appears ("223afe??").
' or address    when the item has 3 or more characters: it is itself a pattern (same * and ? rules)
' for the handler address, not its code ("??e0*" = handler in ROM at $xxE0xxxx, "00000000"), and no
' second item follows.
' The first failing test skips the rest of the record (two items per remaining test).
' result    read when every test matched: "-n" = a virus, vector_check_code = -VAL(n) (decimal; shown with !!!);
' "+hex" = a known program whose XBRA-style link to the previous handler is at handler-8;
' plain hex = a known program, previous handler at handler-4 (normal XBRA). Hex values above $800 get
' $800 added. 1-1000 are names of known programs/TOS (1 = the ROM), above 1000 a second name list.
' No matching record: vector_check_code = 0 (unknown).
' Example: "1", "??e0*", "1" = 1 test: handler address $xxE0xxxx (ROM); result 1.
resvector_patterns_other:
DATA 1,??e0*,1,1,??fa*,1,1,??fc*,1,1,00000000,1,1,00000526,1,*
