DATA 174,175!!1936!!176!!109!!177!!41!!178!!5!!179!!6!!180!!190!!181!!866!!182,183,184,199,185,186,***
' Boot sector records: the first table check_boot_sector RESTOREs, so every boot sector is tested against it.
' Every DATA item is a zero-terminated string. A record is:
' test item [value item], test item [value item], ... "@"+result, owner code, name
' All tests must match, then the record is the diagnosis; a failed record is skipped up to its "@" and its two items.
' Test item, by its first character (the offset into the boot sector):
' ""=$100 "q"=0 "f"=4 "n"=$A "v"=$22 "1"=$30 "2"=$40 "4"=$60 "3"=$80 "6"=$90 "7"=$A0 "h"=$100 "u"=$104 "a"=$10A
' "8"=$120 "j"=$122 "5"=$180
' "!"+b = offset b (0-255);  CHR$(1)+b = offset $100+b (2-byte CVI);  any other character keeps the last offset.
' These are followed by a value item and compare a long, except a 2- or 3-byte value, which compares a word:
' 2 bytes = word (CVI); 4 bytes = long (CVL); 3 bytes = flag byte + word; 5 bytes = flag byte + long. In the flag
' byte, bit 3+i set means data byte i is stored one higher than its value (so 0 bytes can be in the DATA).
' 1 byte = preset long: "g"=$12123456 "h"=$20202020 "i"=$46FC2700 "j"=$6000001E; other lengths keep the last value.
' Tests that carry their value inside the item (compare a long):
' "z": offset = branch target of the first word, DPEEK(0)-$5FFE (2+BRA.S displacement). "z" alone: value 0; "z"+digit:
' preset "1"=$46FC2700 "2"=$3F3C000A "3"=$3F3C0004 "4"=$3F3C0002 "5"=$3F3C0009 "6"=$41F88240 "7"=$42788240
' "8"=$4FF90007 "9"=$4FF90008; "z"+4 bytes: CVL; "z"+flag+4 bytes: escaped long.
' "y"/"x": offset = DPEEK(4)-$5FFA, the BRA.S target of the word at offset 4, plus a step; "y" sets the step to 0
' (offset clamped to >=0), "x" adds 4 first. "Y"/"X": the same with DPEEK(6)-$5FF6. Value: 4 bytes or flag+4 bytes
' after the code character.
' "w": no value, always matches, adds 2 to the step.
' Note: when a record fails, codes "w" to "z" are skipped without a value item and all others with one, so "X"/"Y"
' (which carry their value) would make the skip read one item too many.
' End of record: "@" alone = result 0, "@"+c = result code c. Then the owner code (a single character: index ASC-65 into
' the owner_names_codes_* tables, e.g. "A"=Psygnosis'; "" = "a", or "Ocean's" for result 0; longer strings are used as
' they are) and the name (CHR$(255) is replaced by " disk ", "_" by "demo", "" means "virus free").
' Result codes (the diagnosis alert): 0/"1"/"7" OK disk ("7": the game 'Virus' note); "j" OK, name + " (Cr)"; "h"
' harmless (anti-virus), may be killed; "9" anti-virus, "f" anti-virus with an update note; "i" MS-DOS compatible;
' "e"/"2"/"8"/"3" virus, repair (kill) ("e" Ghost note, "8" German pre-Blitter TOS note, "3" key set); "5" virus that
' also damaged the BPB, BPB repair offered; "6" BPB damaged by a Mutant Signum; "4" Milzbrand damage; "d"/"a" immunized
' the old way; "b" immunized the new way; "g" magic longwords (resident code $12123456), repair/write/print; "c" plain
' boot sector, BPB sanity check.
' Table switches, single items at the start of a record: "s" picks a chain by DPEEK(0): $601C ->
' boot_records_bra_1c_first, $6038 -> boot_records_bra_38_first, $601E -> boot_records_bra_1e_first, other $60xx ->
' boot_records_bra_other_first, else boot_records_word_* by the first digit of HEX$(DPEEK(0)). "c", "e", "t", "o" pick
' boot_records_bra_1c_*, _bra_1e_*, _bra_38_*, _bra_other_* by the first digit of HEX$(LPEEK(branch target)). "r" goes
' to boot_records_last. This table ends with "s".
boot_records_first:
