' Link virus records, read by check_file_link_virus. Every item is a zero-terminated string. A record is:
' "@", name, n (decimal count of tests), n tests of 4 items, action
' Each test: type, offset, length, value.
' type: "" or "1" = compare at file offset; "2"/"3" = read the long at file offset, add the value, keep it as a
' pointer; "4" = compare at pointer+offset.
' offset: hex; "" = $1C (28, the start of the program text after the GEMDOS header); +$200 when cpx_file is set.
' length: hex, 2 = word, else long; "" = 4.
' value: hex; a 4-character item with length 4 is the four bytes themselves (e.g. "VIRU").
' Action (read only when all n tests match): 0 = not a virus after all, 1 = infected by the named link virus, 2 =
' suspicious file start (LEA/PEA), 3 = compressed, the name is the packer, 4 = archive, the name is the archive type. A
' name item "" ends the table.
